{
  "activity_uuid": "activity_916629a2-5def-558c-9fff-80ed3dcaa7be",
  "name": "12.3 Exterior angles of triangles",
  "activity_type": "TYPE_DYNAMIC",
  "activity_sub_type": "SUBTYPE_DYNAMIC_PAGE",
  "content": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 1
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Exterior angles of triangles"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Learning objective: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Identify an exterior angle and use its relationship to interior angles and exterior-angle sum."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Understand the concept"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Extend one side of a triangle at a vertex. The adjoining outside angle is an exterior angle. It and the interior angle at that vertex form a straight line and sum to 180°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Taking one exterior angle at each vertex in a consistent direction gives a total of 360°: three straight angles total 540°, and the interior angles total 180°. The exterior angle at a vertex also equals the sum of the two nonadjacent interior angles."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "blockMathEquation",
        "attrs": {
          "math_equation": "\\text{Interior angle}+\\text{Exterior angle}=180^\\circ"
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "blockImage",
        "attrs": {
          "blockObject": {
            "block_uuid": "block_15afe0b6-12d3-5503-ab6b-c37233ab5379",
            "content": {
              "file_id": "2514e5b9-8337-59ab-963f-552a34ddd065",
              "file_format": "png",
              "activity_uuid": "activity_916629a2-5def-558c-9fff-80ed3dcaa7be"
            }
          },
          "size": {
            "width": 765
          },
          "alignment": "center",
          "unsplash_url": null,
          "unsplash_photographer_name": null,
          "unsplash_photographer_url": null,
          "unsplash_photo_url": null
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Extending a side forms an exterior angle supplementary to the interior angle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Worked examples"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 1: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The interior angle at a vertex is 74°. Find its exterior angle."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "180 − 74 = 106°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Example 2: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A triangle has exterior angles 105°, 135° and x°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Solution: ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "x = 360 − 105 − 135 = 120°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Independent practice"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work these out in your notebook before looking at the self-check below."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Two remote interior angles are 48° and 62°. Find the exterior angle at the third vertex."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Find the missing exterior angle if two others are 95° and 145°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Self-check"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Compare your method and answer. If you are unsure, revisit the relevant worked example before taking the chapter checkpoint."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "110°."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2. ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "bold"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "120°."
          }
        ]
      },
